---
/**
 * UndoToast — the page-level mount point for catalog `pattern-undo-toast`.
 *
 * Render it ONCE per page; drive it from `undoToast.ts` (`showUndoToast`). It is deliberately a
 * sibling of everything else, pinned to the viewport by daisyUI's own `toast` positioner, so nothing
 * can hide it by hiding its parent — the mistake `PanelHost` records in its own header, where the
 * toast lived inside a wrap that goes `hidden` at exactly the moment the undo is needed.
 *
 * BUILT FROM THE CATALOG, WITH NO CLASS FAMILY OF ITS OWN. `toast toast-bottom toast-center` is the
 * daisyUI primitive; the pill, its colours and the ghost Undo button are utilities on the design
 * tokens; the ONLY bespoke CSS is the countdown keyframe, which is a keyframe name and not a
 * component nobody else can reuse. That is the point: a fourth `.xx-*` family for a pattern the
 * catalog already documents would have made the census read `118` where it reads `117`, and this
 * component exists to REMOVE variance, not to add a prefix.
 *
 * Geometry and colour deliberately match `PanelHost`'s `.ph-undo` to the pixel — neutral pill,
 * 12/16 padding, 12px radius, 13px text, a 2px primary bar draining from the left. Two toasts that
 * look like two components is exactly the variance this repo is trying to remove; the difference is
 * that this one is callable from a page that mounts no panel host.
 */
---

<div class="toast toast-bottom toast-center z-[600]" data-undo-toast hidden>
  <div role="status" aria-live="polite" class="relative flex items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-neutral px-4 py-3 text-[length:var(--t-13)] text-neutral-content shadow-lg">
    <span class="iconify lucide--rotate-ccw size-4" data-undo-toast-ic aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden text-ellipsis" data-undo-toast-label></span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost text-primary" data-undo-toast-act hidden></button>
    {/* The bar is a DEADLINE, so `undoToast.ts` draws it only when there is an action to be late
        for, and animates a TRANSFORM — animating width would reflow the pill every frame. */}
    <span class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 h-[2px] origin-left bg-primary" data-undo-toast-bar aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </div>
</div>

<style is:global>
  /* `is:global` because the bar's animation is assigned from `undoToast.ts` at runtime, and a scoped
     keyframe would not be in scope for a style set on the element by script. Uniquely prefixed. */
  @keyframes baseout-undo-countdown { from { transform: scaleX(1); } to { transform: scaleX(0); } }
  /* Reduced motion gets a STATIC FULL BAR, not an absent one — the deadline is still information,
     it just stops moving. The bar carries NO inline transform for this reason: the first version
     set `style="transform: scaleX(0)"` on the element, and an inline declaration beats this rule,
     so reduced-motion users saw no bar at all. Nothing needs the hidden initial state — the toast
     is `hidden` until `showUndoToast` runs, and that assigns the animation in the same call. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    [data-undo-toast-bar] { animation: none !important; transform: scaleX(1); }
  }
</style>
